{"id":15418,"date":"2023-04-18T14:13:00","date_gmt":"2023-04-18T20:13:00","guid":{"rendered":"https:\/\/www.rethinkbehavioralhealth.com\/?post_type=resources&#038;p=15418"},"modified":"2024-03-01T11:55:42","modified_gmt":"2024-03-01T18:55:42","slug":"importance-relationships-practice-behavior-analysis","status":"publish","type":"resources","link":"https:\/\/www.rethinkbehavioralhealth.com\/resources\/importance-relationships-practice-behavior-analysis\/","title":{"rendered":"The Importance of Relationships in the Practice of Behavior Analysis"},"content":{"rendered":"\t\t<div data-elementor-type=\"wp-post\" data-elementor-id=\"15418\" class=\"elementor elementor-15418\" data-elementor-post-type=\"resources\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t<section class=\"elementor-section elementor-top-section elementor-element elementor-element-eef08de elementor-section-boxed elementor-section-height-default elementor-section-height-default\" data-id=\"eef08de\" data-element_type=\"section\" data-settings=\"{&quot;jet_parallax_layout_list&quot;:[]}\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-container elementor-column-gap-default\">\n\t\t\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-column elementor-col-100 elementor-top-column elementor-element elementor-element-8525a46\" data-id=\"8525a46\" data-element_type=\"column\">\n\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-widget-wrap elementor-element-populated\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-c92b414 elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\" data-id=\"c92b414\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"text-editor.default\">\n\t\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-widget-container\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<h2 style=\"margin-top: 0;\">About this Webinar<\/h2><p>Drs. Bridget Taylor &amp; Linda LeBlanc discuss why relationship variables such as empathy and compassion are essential to building strong therapeutic relationships with clients and caregivers and are essential to a core principle of the Ethics Code of Behavior Analysts. Learn how attending to these variables can have a positive impact on caregiver engagement and client outcomes.<\/p><p><em><strong>This webinar is eligible for 1 Ethics CE.<\/strong><\/em><\/p><p><a href=\"https:\/\/behaviorlive.com\/courses\/the-importance-of-relationships-in-the-practice-of-behavior-analysis\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>View On-Demand Webinar<\/strong><\/a><\/p><h3>Our Next Guest: A Conversation with Drs. Bridget Taylor &amp; Linda LeBlanc<\/h3><p>Join us for a lively conversation with Dr. Linda LeBlanc as we discuss the importance of relationship variables in our work as clinicians and supervisors. We will review the ethical implications of attending to relationship variables when working with clients and caregivers and discuss recent research identifying the core responses when building therapeutic relationships.<\/p><h2>Learning Objectives<\/h2><p>At the conclusion of the presentation, participants will be able to:<\/p><ol><li>Identify the importance of relationship variables in the practice of behavior analysis.<\/li><li>Identify core responses that comprise compassion and empathy.<\/li><li>Identify ethical implications in building therapeutic relationships with caregivers.<\/li><\/ol><h2>About the Guest Speaker<\/h2>\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t<\/section>\n\t\t\t\t<section class=\"elementor-section elementor-top-section elementor-element elementor-element-11edf53 authorSection elementor-section-boxed elementor-section-height-default elementor-section-height-default\" data-id=\"11edf53\" data-element_type=\"section\" data-settings=\"{&quot;jet_parallax_layout_list&quot;:[]}\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-container elementor-column-gap-default\">\n\t\t\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-column elementor-col-33 elementor-top-column elementor-element elementor-element-566290b\" data-id=\"566290b\" data-element_type=\"column\">\n\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-widget-wrap elementor-element-populated\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-6377cc4 elementor-widget elementor-widget-image\" data-id=\"6377cc4\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"image.default\">\n\t\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-widget-container\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<img fetchpriority=\"high\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"800\" height=\"800\" src=\"https:\/\/www.rethinkbehavioralhealth.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2023\/04\/dr-linda-leblanc-rethinkbh-our-next-guest.jpg\" class=\"attachment-full size-full wp-image-15337\" alt=\"Dr. Linda LeBlanc\" srcset=\"https:\/\/www.rethinkbehavioralhealth.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2023\/04\/dr-linda-leblanc-rethinkbh-our-next-guest.jpg 800w, https:\/\/www.rethinkbehavioralhealth.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2023\/04\/dr-linda-leblanc-rethinkbh-our-next-guest-300x300.jpg 300w, https:\/\/www.rethinkbehavioralhealth.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2023\/04\/dr-linda-leblanc-rethinkbh-our-next-guest-150x150.jpg 150w, https:\/\/www.rethinkbehavioralhealth.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2023\/04\/dr-linda-leblanc-rethinkbh-our-next-guest-768x768.jpg 768w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 800px) 100vw, 800px\" \/>\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-column elementor-col-66 elementor-top-column elementor-element elementor-element-3dbd981\" data-id=\"3dbd981\" data-element_type=\"column\">\n\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-widget-wrap elementor-element-populated\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-2f9a10e elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\" data-id=\"2f9a10e\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"text-editor.default\">\n\t\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-widget-container\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<h3>Linda A. LeBlanc, Ph.D., BCBA-D, Licensed Psychologist<\/h3><p><span style=\"color: #333333;\">President of LeBlanc Behavioral Consulting<\/span><\/p><p>Her 25 year career has included being past Editor in Chief of the Journal of Applied Behavior Analysis, academic positions at Claremont McKenna College, Western Michigan University and Auburn University as well leadership positions in human services organizations. She established <a href=\"http:\/\/www.lbehavioral.com\/about.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">LeBlanc Behavioral Consulting<\/a> in 2017 and consults to technology companies, universities, and behavior analytic human service organizations. Her professional interests include behavioral treatments, supervision and mentoring, and ethics. She is a Fellow of ABAI and is the 2016 recipient of the APA Nathan H. Azrin Award for Distinguished Contribution in Applied Behavior Analysis.<\/p>\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t<\/section>\n\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t","protected":false},"author":19,"featured_media":19202,"template":"","meta":{"_seopress_robots_primary_cat":"","_seopress_titles_title":"1 CE Webinar: Relationships Importance in Behavior Analysis","_seopress_titles_desc":"On-demand webinar of how attending to relationship variables such as empathy &amp; compassion can have a positive impact on caregiver engagement &amp; client outcomes. ","_seopress_robots_index":"","om_disable_all_campaigns":false,"_links_to":"","_links_to_target":""},"audience":[70],"resource-type":[72],"resource-topic":[329,230],"resource-tag":[268,287,167,103],"class_list":["post-15418","resources","type-resources","status-publish","has-post-thumbnail","hentry","audience-providers","resource-type-webinar","resource-topic-behavior","resource-topic-research","resource-tag-caregiver","resource-tag-continuing-education","resource-tag-engagement","resource-tag-objective"],"_links":{"self":[{"href":"https:\/\/www.rethinkbehavioralhealth.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/resources\/15418","targetHints":{"allow":["GET"]}}],"collection":[{"href":"https:\/\/www.rethinkbehavioralhealth.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/resources"}],"about":[{"href":"https:\/\/www.rethinkbehavioral